#HELP_BEGIN
UDP Broadcast and Receive v2.0

Discovery beacon for 4-Series. Broadcasts MAC,UID,Data to 255.255.255.255
and receives on the same port. Own packets are ignored. Adds a timed announce
and Packet_Rx after the received strings are written. Unicast reply is off
unless enabled, and then answers each sender only once.

Wire format (no spaces): MAC,UID,Data
Example: 00:00:00:00:00:00,123456789,[Type]value
Maximum datagram 306 bytes (17 + 1 + 32 + 1 + 255).

v1.3 is unchanged. This is a new symbol.


Signal Descriptions:

  DIGITAL_INPUT Enable
    Latched. High opens the UDP socket on UDP_Port. Low closes it.

  DIGITAL_INPUT Retrigger
    Pulse to send the current MAC, UID, and Data now, even when Data is empty.
    Ignored unless the socket is open.

  STRING_INPUT Mac[17]
    MAC in the outbound packet. 12 hex digits, or 17 bytes with : or - separators.
    Stored with colon separators. The timed announce waits until this looks like a MAC.

  STRING_INPUT UID[32]
    Unique id in the outbound packet. Letters, digits, hyphen, underscore, up to 32 bytes.

  STRING_INPUT Data[255]
    Payload. A change sends a packet when Data is non-empty and the socket is open.

  DIGITAL_OUTPUT Enable_FB
    High while the listen socket is open on the broadcast address.

  DIGITAL_OUTPUT Packet_Rx
    Pulses for 0.05 s after an accepted packet has been written to Received_IP,
    Received_MAC, Received_UID, and Received_Data. Wire this to UDP Extract Data v2.0.

  STRING_OUTPUT Received_IP
    Sender IP of the last accepted packet.

  STRING_OUTPUT Received_MAC
    MAC parsed from the last accepted packet, colon-separated when recognized.

  STRING_OUTPUT Received_UID
    UID parsed from the last accepted packet.

  STRING_OUTPUT Received_Data
    Data parsed from the last accepted packet, or the whole payload when the
    packet is not a structured MAC,UID,Data datagram.

  INTEGER_PARAMETER UDP_Port
    Port for broadcast and receive (1024-65535, default 50001).

  INTEGER_PARAMETER Enforce_Format
    0d = No enforcement (default). Clear the received outputs, then fill the
         fields that matched. If nothing looks like a MAC or UID, Received_IP
         and Received_Data get the sender IP and the entire payload.
    1d = Enforce MAC,UID,Data. Any other datagram is ignored.

  INTEGER_PARAMETER Announce_Interval
    unitTime. While Enable is high, resend the current packet on this period.
    0s = off (Retrigger and a non-empty Data change still send). Default 5s.
    The first announce goes out as soon as the socket is open and Mac is valid.
    Maximum 600s.
    Every processor running this module receives every announce. On a network
    of hundreds of processors, use 15s or 30s. 5s from 200 processors is about
    40 datagrams a second at each processor.

  INTEGER_PARAMETER Reply
    0d = Off (default). Leave this off when many processors announce. The
         broadcast already tells every peer who you are. A reply to every
         announce would be one packet per pair.
    1d = Unicast reply. Answer a sender once, the first time that IP is seen,
         then not again until that IP has been silent for 60s. At most one
         reply every 0.5 s. 128 senders are remembered; a sender past that
         gets no unicast and still hears the broadcast.
         SIMPL+ has one destination per UDP socket, so the listen socket is
         pointed at the sender for that reply and then restored to
         255.255.255.255. A datagram in that gap can be missed.


Receive parsing (No enforcement) matches v1.3:
  1. Clear all four received outputs.
  2. Write Received_IP when the sender IP is known.
  3. Full MAC,UID,Data fills MAC, UID, and Data.
  4. MAC but not UID: fill MAC and treat the remainder as Data.
  5. Otherwise Received_Data is the entire payload.

Own packets (payload equals what this module would send, or MAC + UID match)
never update the outputs and never get a reply.

MAC shape: 12 hex digits, or 17 bytes as six hex pairs separated by : or -.
UID shape: 1-32 bytes, letters, digits, hyphen, or underscore.

-- VERSION HISTORY --
v2.0  2026-10-19
- Announce_Interval heartbeat (0s off, default 5s). Use 15s or 30s when
  hundreds of processors share the port
- Reply off by default. On answers each new sender once, then waits through
  60s of silence, and sends at most one reply every 0.5 s
- Packet_Rx pulses after the four received strings are written
- Re-open the socket if Enable is high and the listen socket drops

v1.3  2026-09-09
- Prior symbol, left in the tree unchanged

#HELP_END

/* COMPILER DIRECTIVES */

#CATEGORY "46" "TCP/IP" // Custom
#DEFAULT_VOLATILE
#DEFINE_CONSTANT BROADCAST_IP "255.255.255.255"
#DEFINE_CONSTANT HOLD_SLOTS 128
#DEFINE_CONSTANT QUEUE_SLOTS 8
#DEFINE_CONSTANT REPLY_GAP 50
#DEFINE_CONSTANT REPLY_MEMORY 6000
//#ENABLE_TRACE

/* INPUTS & OUTPUTS */

DIGITAL_INPUT	_SKIP_, _SKIP_, _SKIP_, _SKIP_, Enable, Retrigger, _SKIP_, _SKIP_;
STRING_INPUT	_SKIP_, Mac[17], UID[32], Data[255];

DIGITAL_OUTPUT	_SKIP_, _SKIP_, _SKIP_, _SKIP_, Enable_FB, _SKIP_, _SKIP_, Packet_Rx;
STRING_OUTPUT	Received_IP, Received_MAC, Received_UID, Received_Data;

INTEGER_PARAMETER	UDP_Port, Enforce_Format, Announce_Interval, Reply;

/* PROPERTIES */

#BEGIN_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES UDP_Port
	propValidUnits =		unitDecimal;
	propDefaultUnit =		unitDecimal;
	propBounds =			1024d, 65535d;
	propDefaultValue =		50001d;
	propShortDescription =	"UDP port";
#END_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES

#BEGIN_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES Enforce_Format
	propValidUnits =		unitDecimal;
	propDefaultUnit =		unitDecimal;
	propDefaultValue =		0d;
	propList =				{0d, "No enforcement"},
							{1d, "Enforce MAC,UID,Data"};
	propShortDescription =	"Require incoming packets to be MAC,UID,Data";
#END_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES

#BEGIN_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES Announce_Interval
	propValidUnits =		unitTime;
	propDefaultUnit =		unitTime;
	propBounds =			0s, 600s;
	propDefaultValue =		5s;
	propShortDescription =	"Announce period. 0s sends only on Retrigger or Data.";
#END_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES

#BEGIN_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES Reply
	propValidUnits =		unitDecimal;
	propDefaultUnit =		unitDecimal;
	propDefaultValue =		0d;
	propList =				{0d, "Off"},
							{1d, "Once per new sender"};
	propShortDescription =	"Off when many processors announce. On answers a new sender once.";
#END_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES

/* GLOBAL VARIABLES */

UDP_SOCKET	UDPSocket[306];
INTEGER		SocketOpen, SocketBusy, NeedPulse, ReplyCount, AnnounceLeft, ReopenLeft,
			ReplyWait, HoldAge[128];
/* ReplyQ and HoldIP: first bracket is the count, second is the length. */
STRING		RxBuf[306], TxPacket[306], ReplyQ[8][16], HoldIP[128][16];

/* FUNCTIONS */

INTEGER_FUNCTION IsHexChar(INTEGER c) {
	If ((c >= 48) && (c <= 57)) Return (1);	/* 0-9 */
	If ((c >= 65) && (c <= 70)) Return (1);	/* A-F */
	If ((c >= 97) && (c <= 102)) Return (1);	/* a-f */
	Return (0);
}

INTEGER_FUNCTION IsUidChar(INTEGER c) {
	If ((c >= 48) && (c <= 57)) Return (1);	/* 0-9 */
	If ((c >= 65) && (c <= 90)) Return (1);	/* A-Z */
	If ((c >= 97) && (c <= 122)) Return (1);	/* a-z */
	If (c = 45) Return (1);	/* hyphen */
	If (c = 95) Return (1);	/* underscore */
	Return (0);
}

INTEGER_FUNCTION LooksLikeMAC(STRING srcStr) {
	INTEGER i, sep, ch, n;

	n = LEN(srcStr);
	If (n = 12) {
		For (i = 1 to 12) {
			ch = BYTE(srcStr, i);
			If (IsHexChar(ch) = 0) Return (0);
		}
		Return (1);
	}

	If (n = 17) {
		sep = BYTE(srcStr, 3);
		If ((sep <> 58) && (sep <> 45)) Return (0);	/* : or - */
		ch = BYTE(srcStr, 6);
		If (ch <> sep) Return (0);
		ch = BYTE(srcStr, 9);
		If (ch <> sep) Return (0);
		ch = BYTE(srcStr, 12);
		If (ch <> sep) Return (0);
		ch = BYTE(srcStr, 15);
		If (ch <> sep) Return (0);
		For (i = 1 to 17) {
			If ((i <> 3) && (i <> 6) && (i <> 9) && (i <> 12) && (i <> 15)) {
				ch = BYTE(srcStr, i);
				If (IsHexChar(ch) = 0) Return (0);
			}
		}
		Return (1);
	}

	Return (0);
}

INTEGER_FUNCTION LooksLikeUID(STRING srcStr) {
	INTEGER i, ch, n;

	n = LEN(srcStr);
	If ((n = 0) || (n > 32)) Return (0);
	For (i = 1 to n) {
		ch = BYTE(srcStr, i);
		If (IsUidChar(ch) = 0) Return (0);
	}
	Return (1);
}

STRING_FUNCTION FormatMAC(STRING tempMAC) {
	STRING temp[17];

	If (LEN(tempMAC) = 17) {
		If (FIND(":", tempMAC))
			Return (tempMAC);
		Else {
			MakeString(temp, "%s:%s:%s:%s:%s:%s", Mid(tempMAC, 1, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 4, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 7, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 10, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 13, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 16, 2));
			Return (temp);
		}
	}

	Else If (LEN(tempMAC) = 12) {
		MakeString(temp, "%s:%s:%s:%s:%s:%s", Mid(tempMAC, 1, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 3, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 5, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 7, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 9, 2), Mid(tempMAC, 11, 2));
		Return (temp);
	}

	Else {
		TRACE("[UDP]: MAC address error, incorrect length (%u) for \x22%s\x22", LEN(tempMAC), tempMAC);
		Return ("00:00:00:00:00:00");
	}
}

INTEGER_FUNCTION PacketIsSelf(STRING srcMAC, STRING srcUID) {
	STRING mine[306], localMAC[17], packetMAC[17];
	INTEGER isMac;

	localMAC = FormatMAC(Mac);
	MakeString(mine, "%s,%s,%s", localMAC, UID, Data);
	If (RxBuf = mine) Return (1);

	If ((LEN(Mac) = 0) && (LEN(UID) = 0)) Return (0);

	isMac = LooksLikeMAC(srcMAC);
	packetMAC = FormatMAC(srcMAC);
	If ((isMac = 1) && (packetMAC = localMAC) && (srcUID = UID))
		Return (1);

	Return (0);
}

FUNCTION BuildPacket() {
	MakeString(TxPacket, "%s,%s,%s", FormatMAC(Mac), UID, Data);
}

FUNCTION OpenSocket() {
	SIGNED_INTEGER status;

	If (SocketBusy = 1) Return;

	If (SocketOpen = 1) {
		SocketUDP_Disable(UDPSocket);
		SocketOpen = 0;
		Enable_FB = 0;
	}

	status = SocketUDP_Enable(UDPSocket, BROADCAST_IP, UDP_Port);
	If (status < 0) {
		SocketOpen = 0;
		Enable_FB = 0;
		TRACE("[UDP]: Failed to open UDP socket (error %d)", status);
	}
	Else {
		SocketOpen = 1;
		Enable_FB = 1;
		AnnounceLeft = 0;
		TRACE("[UDP]: Opened UDP Socket successfully");
	}
}

FUNCTION CloseSocket() {
	SIGNED_INTEGER status;

	If (SocketBusy = 1) Return;

	If (SocketOpen = 1) {
		status = SocketUDP_Disable(UDPSocket);
		If (status < 0) TRACE("[UDP]: Failed to close UDP socket (error %d)", status);
		Else TRACE("[UDP]: Closed UDP Socket");
	}
	SocketOpen = 0;
	Enable_FB = 0;
}

INTEGER_FUNCTION SendBroadcast(INTEGER allowEmptyData) {
	SIGNED_INTEGER status;

	If (SocketOpen = 0) {
		TRACE("[UDP]: Send ignored, socket is not open");
		Return (0);
	}
	If (SocketBusy = 1) Return (0);

	If ((allowEmptyData = 0) && (LEN(Data) = 0)) Return (0);

	BuildPacket();
	status = SocketSend(UDPSocket, TxPacket);
	If (status < 0) {
		TRACE("[UDP]: SocketSend failed (error %d)", status);
		Return (0);
	}
	TRACE("[UDP]: Sent: %s", TxPacket);
	Return (1);
}

INTEGER_FUNCTION FindHold(STRING ip) {
	INTEGER i;

	For (i = 1 to HOLD_SLOTS) {
		If ((LEN(HoldIP[i]) > 0) && (HoldIP[i] = ip)) Return (i);
	}
	Return (0);
}

INTEGER_FUNCTION FreeHold() {
	INTEGER i;

	For (i = 1 to HOLD_SLOTS) {
		If (LEN(HoldIP[i]) = 0) Return (i);
	}
	Return (0);
}

FUNCTION RememberHold(STRING ip) {
	INTEGER slot;

	slot = FindHold(ip);
	If (slot > 0) HoldAge[slot] = 0;
}

FUNCTION AgeHolds(INTEGER elapsed) {
	INTEGER i;

	For (i = 1 to HOLD_SLOTS) {
		If (LEN(HoldIP[i]) > 0) {
			HoldAge[i] = HoldAge[i] + elapsed;
			If (HoldAge[i] >= REPLY_MEMORY) {
				HoldIP[i] = "";
				HoldAge[i] = 0;
			}
		}
	}
}

FUNCTION QueueReply(STRING ip) {
	INTEGER slot;

	If (Reply <> 1) Return;
	If (LEN(ip) = 0) Return;
	If (ip = BROADCAST_IP) Return;
	If (ip = "0.0.0.0") Return;

	slot = FindHold(ip);
	If (slot > 0) {
		HoldAge[slot] = 0;
		Return;
	}
	If (ReplyCount >= QUEUE_SLOTS) Return;

	slot = FreeHold();
	If (slot = 0) {
		TRACE("[UDP]: Reply table full, no unicast for %s", ip);
		Return;
	}
	HoldIP[slot] = ip;
	HoldAge[slot] = 0;
	ReplyCount = ReplyCount + 1;
	ReplyQ[ReplyCount] = ip;
}

FUNCTION SendUnicast(STRING destIP) {
	SIGNED_INTEGER status;

	If (SocketOpen = 0) Return;
	If (SocketBusy = 1) Return;
	If (LEN(destIP) = 0) Return;

	SocketBusy = 1;
	BuildPacket();

	status = SocketUDP_Disable(UDPSocket);
	If (status < 0) TRACE("[UDP]: Reply disable failed (error %d)", status);

	status = SocketUDP_Enable(UDPSocket, destIP, UDP_Port);
	If (status < 0) {
		TRACE("[UDP]: Reply open failed for %s (error %d)", destIP, status);
	}
	Else {
		status = SocketSend(UDPSocket, TxPacket);
		If (status < 0) TRACE("[UDP]: Reply send failed to %s (error %d)", destIP, status);
		Else {
			TRACE("[UDP]: Replied to %s: %s", destIP, TxPacket);
			RememberHold(destIP);
		}
		SocketUDP_Disable(UDPSocket);
	}

	status = SocketUDP_Enable(UDPSocket, BROADCAST_IP, UDP_Port);
	If (status < 0) {
		SocketOpen = 0;
		Enable_FB = 0;
		TRACE("[UDP]: Failed to restore broadcast socket (error %d)", status);
	}
	Else {
		SocketOpen = 1;
		Enable_FB = 1;
	}
	SocketBusy = 0;
}

FUNCTION DrainOneReply() {
	INTEGER i;
	STRING dest[16];

	If (ReplyCount = 0) Return;
	If (ReplyWait > 0) Return;
	If ((SocketOpen = 0) || (SocketBusy = 1)) Return;

	dest = ReplyQ[1];
	For (i = 1 to ReplyCount - 1) ReplyQ[i] = ReplyQ[i + 1];
	ReplyQ[ReplyCount] = "";
	ReplyCount = ReplyCount - 1;
	SendUnicast(dest);
	ReplyWait = REPLY_GAP;
}

FUNCTION ClearReceived() {
	Received_IP = "";
	Received_MAC = "";
	Received_UID = "";
	Received_Data = "";
}

/* EVENT HANDLERS */

CHANGE Enable {
	If (Enable = 1) OpenSocket();
	Else CloseSocket();
}

PUSH Retrigger {
	SendBroadcast(1);
}

CHANGE Data {
	SendBroadcast(0);
}

SOCKETRECEIVE UDPSocket {
	INTEGER pos1, pos2, gotMAC, gotUID, fullPacket;
	SIGNED_INTEGER status;
	STRING buffer[306], srcIP[15], srcMAC[17], srcUID[32], srcData[306];
	STRING field1[306], field2[306], field3[306], formattedMAC[17];

	buffer = UDPSocket.SocketRxBuf;
	ClearBuffer(UDPSocket.SocketRxBuf);
	RxBuf = buffer;

	TRACE("[UDP]: Socket received raw: %s", buffer);

	srcIP = "";
	srcMAC = "";
	srcUID = "";
	srcData = "";
	gotMAC = 0;
	gotUID = 0;
	fullPacket = 0;

	status = SocketGetSenderIPAddress(UDPSocket, srcIP);
	If (status <> 0) {
		srcIP = "";
		TRACE("[UDP]: Failed to retrieve sender's IP (error: %d)", status);
	}

	pos1 = FIND(",", buffer);
	pos2 = 0;
	If (pos1 > 0) pos2 = FIND(",", buffer, pos1 + 1);

	If ((pos1 > 0) && (pos2 > 0)) {
		field1 = LEFT(buffer, pos1 - 1);
		field2 = MID(buffer, pos1 + 1, pos2 - (pos1 + 1));
		field3 = MID(buffer, pos2 + 1, LEN(buffer));

		If (LooksLikeMAC(field1) = 1) {
			gotMAC = 1;
			srcMAC = field1;
			If (LooksLikeUID(field2) = 1) {
				gotUID = 1;
				srcUID = field2;
				srcData = field3;
				fullPacket = 1;
			}
			Else {
				srcData = MID(buffer, pos1 + 1, LEN(buffer));
			}
		}
		Else {
			srcData = buffer;
		}
	}
	Else If (pos1 > 0) {
		field1 = LEFT(buffer, pos1 - 1);
		field2 = MID(buffer, pos1 + 1, LEN(buffer));

		If (LooksLikeMAC(field1) = 1) {
			gotMAC = 1;
			srcMAC = field1;
			If (LooksLikeUID(field2) = 1) {
				gotUID = 1;
				srcUID = field2;
			}
			Else {
				srcData = field2;
			}
		}
		Else {
			srcData = buffer;
		}
	}
	Else {
		If (LooksLikeMAC(buffer) = 1) {
			gotMAC = 1;
			srcMAC = buffer;
		}
		Else If (LooksLikeUID(buffer) = 1) {
			gotUID = 1;
			srcUID = buffer;
		}
		Else {
			srcData = buffer;
		}
	}

	If (PacketIsSelf(srcMAC, srcUID) = 1) {
		TRACE("[UDP]: Ignored own packet");
		TerminateEvent;
	}

	If ((Enforce_Format = 1) && (fullPacket = 0)) {
		TRACE("[UDP]: Dropped non-conforming packet (Enforce MAC,UID,Data)");
		TerminateEvent;
	}

	ClearReceived();

	If (LEN(srcIP) > 0) Received_IP = srcIP;

	If (gotMAC = 1) {
		formattedMAC = FormatMAC(srcMAC);
		Received_MAC = formattedMAC;
		TRACE("[UDP]: Parsed Mac: %s", formattedMAC);
	}
	If (gotUID = 1) {
		Received_UID = srcUID;
		TRACE("[UDP]: Parsed UID: %s", srcUID);
	}
	If (LEN(srcData) > 0) {
		Received_Data = srcData;
		TRACE("[UDP]: Parsed Data: %s", srcData);
	}
	Else If ((gotMAC = 0) && (gotUID = 0) && (LEN(buffer) > 0)) {
		Received_Data = buffer;
		TRACE("[UDP]: Unstructured payload as Data: %s", buffer);
	}

	QueueReply(srcIP);
	NeedPulse = 1;
}

/* MAIN */

FUNCTION Main() {
	INTEGER i;

	SocketOpen = 0;
	SocketBusy = 0;
	NeedPulse = 0;
	ReplyCount = 0;
	AnnounceLeft = 0;
	ReopenLeft = 0;
	ReplyWait = 0;
	Enable_FB = 0;
	For (i = 1 to QUEUE_SLOTS) ReplyQ[i] = "";
	For (i = 1 to HOLD_SLOTS) {
		HoldIP[i] = "";
		HoldAge[i] = 0;
	}
	WaitForInitializationComplete();
	If (Enable = 1) OpenSocket();

	WHILE (1) {
		DrainOneReply();
		If (NeedPulse = 1) {
			NeedPulse = 0;
			Pulse(5, Packet_Rx);
		}
		If ((Enable = 1) && (SocketOpen = 0) && (SocketBusy = 0) && (ReopenLeft <= 0)) {
			OpenSocket();
			ReopenLeft = 100;
		}
		If ((SocketOpen = 1) && (Announce_Interval > 0) && (AnnounceLeft <= 0) && (SocketBusy = 0)) {
			If (LooksLikeMAC(Mac) = 1) SendBroadcast(1);
			Else TRACE("[UDP]: Announce waiting for a MAC address");
			AnnounceLeft = Announce_Interval;
		}
		DELAY(1);
		AgeHolds(1);
		If (AnnounceLeft > 0) AnnounceLeft = AnnounceLeft - 1;
		If (ReopenLeft > 0) ReopenLeft = ReopenLeft - 1;
		If (ReplyWait > 0) ReplyWait = ReplyWait - 1;
	}
}
